  "independent_checks": {
    "finite_atlas_support_PD": "Rational-box finite intersections are balls; finite-union induction uses the exact signed support MV ladder. Compact supports, finite cycles and finite bounding chains all enter one finite-union stage. Excision and common-support equality identify both colimits without selecting a countable chart family. Finite supplied-atlas gluing covers noncompact and disconnected scope.",
    "collared_relative_PD": "Collar cores K_d cofinal in the interior; collar push is a homotopy inverse to interior inclusion. Pair five-lemma/excision comparison identifies H*(W,A) with support cohomology; canonical relative orientation class restricts to the core support orientation. Recomputed both connector signs from partial(alpha cap z)=(-1)^p(alpha cap partial z-delta alpha cap z), including (-1)^p adjustment on the homology connector. Four surrounding cap isomorphisms give the second map. Supplied collar, not an additional collar-existence assumption, is used.",
    "boundary_cokernel": "H1(A)->H1(X) injective makes the MV sum onto H2(Y). H2(B)->H2(X) onto kills the X summand modulo outer boundary. MV equality identifies the seam image of W with that killed X image, so the map factors through the entire W boundary quotient. Finite-dimensional rank consequence uses finite elimination only.",
    "subgroup_extension": "Left A submodules supported on a finite set of cosets Hg admit canonical support projections and finite-free coordinates after only finite representative choices. Projection plus coordinate exactness proves flatness for arbitrary modules and complexes; H-support projection is A-bilinear and splits the unit, proving faithfulness. Checked noncommutative common right denominators and product as^-1*bt^-1=au(tv)^-1 when bv=su. Right-coset support separation of q*s=a proves F intersection B=A and injectivity of F/A->K/B as A-bimodules."
  },
